  <note xmi:id="_6JMVMcmCEfClDv2KOrT7rQ" opaque="true" posX="32" posY="32" sizeHeight="65" sizeWidth="609" text="This route demonstrates how JMS messages from a Queue can be &#xD;&#xA;forwarded as requests to a service and responses sent back to JMS.">
    <elementParameter xmi:id="_6JMVMsmCEfClDv2KOrT7rQ" field="TEXT" name="FONT_SIZE" value="11"/>
  </note>
  <note xmi:id="_6JMVM8mCEfClDv2KOrT7rQ" opaque="true" posX="32" posY="256" sizeHeight="193" sizeWidth="609" text="To see that scenario working you need to do following&#xD;&#xA;&#x9;- Export and deploy data service DemoService (from Integration perspective)&#xD;&#xA;&#x9;   to the Talend ESB Runtime.&#xD;&#xA;&#x9;- Start ActiveMQ&#xD;&#xA;&#x9;- Route expects ActiveMQ is started on the localhost, if not please modify the&#xD;&#xA;&#x9;   JMStoHTTP context value.&#xD;&#xA;Scenario includes 3 routes:&#xD;&#xA;&#x9;- JMStoHTTP reads form the IN queue and send responses to the OUT queue&#xD;&#xA;&#x9;- SendToJMS fills the the IN queue&#xD;&#xA;&#x9;- ReceiveFromJMS is reading the OUT queue"/>
